# Vulnerabilities accepted in the image scan (delivery.yml). Every entry needs a reason and an
# expiry: once the date passes, Trivy reports the CVE again and the release gate fails, so the
# entry has to be re-checked instead of staying forever.

# CVE-2026-47884 / GHSA-pc63-qcmh-9cmg (CRITICAL): spring-webmvc improper path limitation in
# XsltView. Only 7.0.9 is patched; no Spring Framework 6.2.x fix is published, and moving to
# Spring Boot 4 / Framework 7 is a separate migration. Not reachable here: no service uses
# XsltView or any server-side view resolver, every MVC endpoint returns JSON (api-gateway runs
# on WebFlux and is not affected). Drop this line and override spring-framework in pom.xml as
# soon as a patched 6.2.x release exists.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-11-05
